              "locator": "Complete 33-page chapter; full relevant section inspected."
            }
          ]
        },
        "strategy": "direct"
      },
      {
        "id": "thm-rpm-h-poincare-moment-map-and-algebra",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Poincare cotangent moment map and full generator algebra",
        "statement": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$. For the group and cotangent conventions of [[def-rpm-h-poincare-charge-space]], the map $\\mu:T^*\\mathbb R^4\\to\\mathfrak g^*$ defined by $\\langle\\mu(x,p),(a,A)\\rangle=\\ell_{(a,A)}(x,p)$ is a smooth equivariant moment map and obeys\n\n$$\\{\\ell_\\xi,\\ell_\\eta\\}=\\ell_{[\\xi,\\eta]},\\quad \\{P^a,P^b\\}=0,\\quad \\{J^{ab},P^c\\}=\\eta^{ac}P^b-\\eta^{bc}P^a,$$\n\n$$\\{J^{ab},J^{cd}\\}=\\eta^{ac}J^{bd}-\\eta^{ad}J^{bc}-\\eta^{bc}J^{ad}+\\eta^{bd}J^{ac}.$$\n\nFor each future massive shell $p_0=-E/c$, $E=\\sqrt{m^2c^4+c^2|\\mathbf p|^2}$, or nonzero future null shell with $m=0$ and $|\\mathbf p|>0$, its Poincare charges descend to the global ray quotient. The induced dual action is $(P,J)\\mapsto(\\Lambda P,\\Lambda J\\Lambda^T+a\\wedge\\Lambda P)$. On the fixed-time slice $x^0=ct$, with physical position $q^i=x^i$, the boost component $B_i=J^{0i}=ct p_i-q^iE/c$ is explicitly time dependent and satisfies $\\partial_tB_i+\\{B_i,E\\}=0$. These are mathematical identities; conservation is conditional on the stated free-shell evolution.",
        "deps": [
          "def-rpm-h-poincare-charge-space",
          "thm-rpm-h-canonical-poisson-and-flow",
          "prop-cotangent-lift-is-hamiltonian-with-tautological-moment-map",
          "thm-rpm-h-flat-shell-global-reduction",
          "thm-rpm-h-inertial-time-reduced-hamiltonian",
          "def-countable-choice"
        ],
