              "title": "Nesta van der Schaaf, Classical and Quantum Particles in Galilean and Poincaré Spacetime, complete 2017 monograph PDF; §9.3 PDF pp. 77–79; §10.2.2 PDF pp. 81–82.",
              "url": "https://www.math.ru.nl/~landsman/Nesta.pdf",
              "locator": "Complete 85-page monograph; full relevant sections inspected. Source uses natural units and signature (+---), translated explicitly in local statements."
            }
          ]
        },
        "strategy": "direct",
        "physical_scope": "Adopt specified KKS phase orbit, primitive m,s, chosen H=cP0; no quantum spectrum/unitary Wigner/spin-supplementary or force law inferred."
      },
      {
        "id": "thm-rpm-h-spinless-kks-identification",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Massive spinless shell reduction is a single KKS orbit",
        "statement": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$. Fix $m>0$. Let $\\Sigma_m^+$ be the future mass shell in flat Minkowski cotangent space and quotient its complete characteristic lines as in the current draft H8 supplier. The resulting global phase space has coordinates $(a^i,p_i)\\in\\mathbb R^6$ and form $da^i\\wedge dp_i$. Under the charge map of [[thm-rpm-h-poincare-moment-map-and-algebra]], it is globally symplectomorphic to the single coadjoint orbit through $(P=(mc,0),J=0)$. Its image is exactly the future massive charge pairs with $P^2=-m^2c^2$ and $W=0$, where $W^a=\\tfrac12\\varepsilon^{abcd}p_bJ_{cd}$. This statement identifies one smooth orbit; it makes no regularity claim about a union of Casimir level sets.",
        "deps": [
          "thm-rpm-h-poincare-moment-map-and-algebra",
          "thm-rpm-h-flat-shell-global-reduction",
