      {
        "id": "pthm-rpm-h-free-symmetry-conservation",
        "kind": "physics-theorem",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Conditional free Poincare and background Killing charges",
        "statement": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ for the moment-map supplier. Adopt either the massive free test-particle action or the distinct massless shell action of [[post-rpm-h-free-test-particle-action]] and [[post-rpm-h-massless-shell-action]]. Conditional on those model choices and the corresponding future free-shell equations, the affine Poincaré charges are conserved on flat spacetime; in a fixed-time Hamiltonian description the boost charge includes its explicit partial-time derivative. On a prescribed curved background, every mechanical scalar $p_a\\xi^a$ for a Killing field is conserved along the adopted free shell. These are model deductions. They do not establish the empirical adequacy of either action, and they do not extend to arbitrary interacting potentials.",
        "deps": [
          "post-rpm-h-free-test-particle-action",
          "post-rpm-h-massless-shell-action",
