        "id": "thm-rpm-h-complete-integral-coordinates",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Complete integrals and covariant versus time Hamilton-Jacobi",
        "statement": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ for the cotangent/HJ supplier chain. Let $H(t,q,p)$ be smooth and let $S(t,q,\\alpha)$ be a $C^3$ solution of $S_t+H(t,q,S_q)=0$ on an open domain. If the mixed matrix $S_{q\\alpha}$ is invertible at $(t,q,\\alpha)$, then after restricting neighborhoods the equations $p=S_q$, $\\beta=S_\\alpha$ define a local canonical transformation $(q,p)\\leftrightarrow(\\alpha,\\beta)$ at each fixed $t$, and $\\beta$ is constant along its Hamilton characteristics. Such a family is a complete integral only on that nonsingular local domain. In a temporal spacetime chart satisfying H9, the covariant future-shell equation $g^{ab}S_aS_b+m^2c^2=0$ reduces to the time Hamilton–Jacobi equation with $p_0=S_t/c=-H/c$; for $m=0$ require a nonzero future null covector. The function $S$ has action units, not dimensionless phase units.",
        "deps": [
          "thm-rpm-h-local-hamilton-jacobi",
