      {
        "id": "pthm-rpm-h-hj-trajectories",
        "kind": "physics-theorem",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Conditional particle trajectories from Hamilton-Jacobi characteristics",
        "statement": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ for the cotangent/H7 supplier chain. Adopt the massive free action or separate massless shell action in [[post-rpm-h-free-test-particle-action]] and [[post-rpm-h-massless-shell-action]]. Let a smooth time Hamiltonian $H(t,q,p)$ describe the corresponding shell in a declared temporal chart, and let $S(t,q)$ be a local classical HJ solution on an actually invertible characteristic projection. Then each curve satisfying $\\dot q=H_p(t,q,S_q)$ with $p=S_q(t,q)$ satisfies Hamilton's equations and, under the matching H7 first-order shell formulation, is a trajectory of the adopted model. The conclusion holds only on the chart and local solution interval; it does not continue through a caustic or assert a global HJ solution. It is a conditional mathematical prediction, not a reported observation.",
