        "id": "cex-rpm-h-instantaneous-potential-free-boost",
        "kind": "counterexample",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Free boost plus instantaneous relativistic pair potential violates the charge algebra",
        "statement": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ for the cited Poincare algebra input. On the product of two one-dimensional equal-time particle phase spaces $(q_a,p_a)$, let $m_a>0$, $E_a(p_a)=\\sqrt{m_a^2c^4+c^2p_a^2}$, $H=E_1+E_2+V(q_1-q_2)$ with $V(r)=kr^2/2$, $k>0$, and retain the free total boost\n\n$$K=\\frac{q_1E_1+q_2E_2}{c^2}-t(p_1+p_2),\\qquad P=p_1+p_2.$$\n\nWith canonical brackets, $\\{K,P\\}=(E_1+E_2)/c^2$, while the Poincaré charge algebra requires $\\{K,P\\}=H/c^2$. They disagree at every configuration with $q_1\\ne q_2$. The construction is therefore a counterexample to combining this instantaneous potential with the unchanged free boost. It is not a universal no-interaction theorem.",
        "deps": [
          "thm-rpm-h-poincare-moment-map-and-algebra",
          "def-rpm-h-poincare-charge-space",
          "def-countable-choice"
        ],
