      {
        "id": "ex-rpm-h-two-shell-consistency-obstruction",
        "kind": "example",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Two scalar shell potentials fail first-class closure generically",
        "statement": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ for the cotangent/constraint supplier. On the product of two Minkowski cotangent spaces, use signature $(-,+,+,+)$, $P_i^a=\\eta^{ab}p_{ib}$, $r=x_1-x_2$, and constraints\n\n$$C_1=\\tfrac12(p_1^2+m_1^2c^2)+V(r^2),\\qquad C_2=\\tfrac12(p_2^2+m_2^2c^2)+V(r^2).$$\n\nHere $m_i>0$, $r^2=\\eta_{ab}r^ar^b$, and $V$ is smooth with units of momentum squared. Their canonical bracket is\n\n$$\\{C_1,C_2\\}=-2V'(r^2)\\,r\\cdot(P_1+P_2).$$\n\nFor $V(z)=\\lambda z$, $\\lambda>0$, this bracket is nonzero at explicit points on the joint surface $C_1=C_2=0$ where $dC_1,dC_2$ are independent. Thus, by [[def-rpm-h-first-class-constraint-family]], the pair fails first-class closure on the local regular surface around each such point, and arbitrary independent multipliers need not preserve both constraints there. Additional consistency conditions are required; no universal obstruction for all interacting relativistic models is claimed.",
        "deps": [
          "thm-rpm-h-constraint-consistency",
          "def-countable-choice",
          "def-rpm-h-first-class-constraint-family",
          "thm-rpm-h-canonical-poisson-and-flow"
        ],
