      {
        "id": "cex-rpm-h-relativistic-hj-caustic",
        "kind": "counterexample",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Smooth free relativistic Hamilton-Jacobi data form a caustic",
        "statement": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ for the cotangent-shell supplier. For the free one-dimensional massive Hamiltonian $H(p)=E(p)=\\sqrt{m^2c^4+c^2p^2}$ with $m>0$, choose smooth initial action $S_0(a)=-\\kappa a^2/2$, $\\kappa>0$ in kg/s. Its characteristics have $p(a)=-\\kappa a$ and\n\n$$q(t,a)=a+t\\frac{c^2p(a)}{E(p(a))}.$$\n\nThe projection derivative is $\\partial_aq=1-t\\kappa m^2c^6/E(p)^3$. It stays positive for $0\\le t<m/\\kappa$ and first vanishes at $(t,a)=(m/\\kappa,0)$, where $\\partial_ap=-\\kappa\\ne0$. Therefore this characteristic family cannot extend there as a smooth single-valued graph $p=S_q(t,q)$ with finite $S_{qq}$. The initial data and Hamiltonian are smooth; the failure is the projection singularity, not an initial-data defect.",
        "deps": [
          "thm-rpm-h-local-hamilton-jacobi",
          "thm-rpm-h-inertial-time-reduced-hamiltonian",
          "def-countable-choice"
        ],
