      {
        "id": "ex-rpm-h-free-relativistic-complete-integral",
        "kind": "example",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Explicit massive and nonzero-null free complete integral",
        "statement": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ for the cotangent-shell supplier. For a free massive particle with $m>0$, or a nonzero massless particle with $m=0$ and $\\alpha\\ne0$, define\n\n$$S(t,q,\\alpha)=q\\cdot\\alpha-tE(\\alpha),\\qquad E(\\alpha)=\\sqrt{m^2c^4+c^2|\\alpha|^2}.$$\n\nThen $S_t+E(S_q)=0$, $S_{q\\alpha}=I$, and its integration coordinates satisfy $\\beta=S_\\alpha=q-tc^2\\alpha/E$, equivalently $q=\\beta+t c^2\\alpha/E$. The mixed Hessian is everywhere nonsingular on the stated domain, so this is a complete integral there. $[S]=\\mathrm{J\\,s}$, $[\\alpha]=\\mathrm{kg\\,m/s}$, and $[\\beta]=\\mathrm m$.",
